'''Damage modifiers''' refer to damage instances that are modified by a percentage or flat value, causing the damage dealt to be increased or decreased. [[Buff]]s or [[debuff]]s usually affect the damage dealt or taken by a unit, while damaging abilities and spells can modify their damage dealt under certain conditions.

It is important to note that damage modifiers do not add '''bonus''' damage but affect all of the damage dealt by an instance. Damage modifiers may also only affect specific damage sub-types ([[physical damage|physical]], [[magic damage|magic]], or [[true damage|true]]).

Buffs or debuffs that modify damage are granted by [[champion ability|abilities]], [[item]]s, [[rune]]s, and [[summoner spell]]s.

== Damage dealt modifier ==
These are [[buff]]s that allow the champion that has them to deal increased or decreased {{tip|physical damage|physical}}, {{tip|magic damage|magic}}, and situationally {{tip|true damage}}. The raw value from the attack or ability is increased or decreased by the modifier and then applied to the target. All damage modifiers {{tip|stacks additively|stack additively}}.
