{{TOCright}}{{as|{{sti|'''Health regeneration'''}}|hp}}, or {{as|{{tt|'''HP5'''|Health per 5 seconds}}|hp}}, is a [[Champion statistic|stat]] that determines the rate that a unit's current [[Health|health]] passively regenerates, measured per 5 seconds as a stat and displayed per 1 second {{tt|on the HUD|When the health bar is hovered.}}. Health regeneration occurs in {{fd|0.5}}-second intervals and is disabled when the unit's current health exactly equals its maximum health.
* Health regeneration '''{{tip|stacks additively}}''', and each point acquired directly adds to the statistic (1:1). ''This is true for both flat values and percentage values''.

Every champion has a certain amount of base health regeneration (excluding {{ci|Briar}}) that increases through [[Champion statistic#Growing statistics|growth per level]]. Effects may consider '''base''' health regeneration or '''bonus''' health regeneration. '''Bonus''' health regeneration can be gained from any source other than levels, for example from [[Champion ability|abilities]], [[Buff|buffs]], [[Item (League of Legends)|items]], [[Rune (League of Legends)|runes]], and others. 

Health regeneration is considered to be a form of [[healing]] only for the purposes of healing modifiers, and for the sake of tracking "Healing Done" at the end-of-game screen.

{{gold value}}
* Percentage '''base health regeneration''' has a gold value of {{g|{{#invoke:Gold value|wikivaluedefine}}{{#var:hp5}}}} per point.
* Health restored by potion has a gold value of {{g|0.4166}} per point.
